      "side": 1,
      "message": "We try to iterate a certain address range of a given process to determine whether the pte-relevant pages should be deactivated, readahead or discarded.\nThe function do_madvise is the interface that tell the kernel how it should handle a particular memory region. As such, we utilize the madvise mechanism to do our readahead operations by exporting this function.\nall other functions are used to do deactivation, readahead or discard operations.\nfunctions: mm_find_pmd, walk_page_range, walk_page_range_novma, walk_page_vma, walk_page_mapping, folio_referenced, are used to iterate through a certain address space to find out the pte-relevant pages that should be readahead.\nfunctions: vm_normal_page, pages_add_anon_rmap, page_add_new_anon_rmap, page_add_file_rmap, page_remove_rmap, are used to allocate page table entries and establish mapping between pages and the ptes, when perform readahead operations.\nthe read_swap_cache_async function is used to read a page from the swap cache asynchronously.\nswap_free, folio_free_swap is used to free a swap slot that the corresponding page has been read into memory already.",
      "parentUuid": "f1db9419_8532740b",
      "revId": "c642e2db80ffd98e60f47adece8adcfa505cdde3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
